8. DIFFERENCE BETWEEN TREE AND BINARY TREE
================================================================================================================

   TREE:

   1. A Tree is a Non-Linear Data Structure.
   2. A Node can have any number of Children.
   3. There is no fixed maximum limit on the number of Children.
   4. It is used to represent hierarchical data.

   BINARY TREE:

   1. A Binary Tree is also a Non-Linear Data Structure.
   2. A Node can have at most TWO Children.
   3. Children are called Left Child and Right Child.
   4. It is used in searching, sorting and hierarchical operations.

   Important:

   Every Binary Tree is a Tree.
   But every Tree is NOT a Binary Tree.


