10. IMPORTANT POINTS TO REMEMBER
================================================================================================================

   1. Tree is a Non-Linear Data Structure.

   2. Binary Tree is a special type of Tree.

   3. Every Binary Tree is a Tree, but every Tree is not a Binary Tree.

   4. Root Node does not have a Parent.

   5. Leaf Node does not have any Children.

   6. Internal Node has at least one Child.

   7. A Binary Tree Node can have a maximum of two Children.

   8. A Tree with N Nodes contains exactly N-1 Edges.

   9. A Tree does not contain any Cycle.

   10. Full Binary Tree: Every Node has either 0 or 2 Children.

   11. Complete Binary Tree: Last Level is filled from Left to Right.

   12. Perfect Binary Tree: All Levels are completely filled.

   13. Balanced Binary Tree: Height difference is at most 1
       at every Node.

   14. Skewed Binary Tree: Every Node has at most one Child.


